        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "9882ddbc-41ee-509f-9fa6-d233ee99a878",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: National Gas Turbine Establishment, Royal Aircraft Establishment, Power Jets, Royal Air Force\n- People: Frank Whittle, Hayne Constant\n- Places: Fleet, United Kingdom\n- Topics: Gas turbine and jet engine design and development\n\nFacts:\n- Frank Whittle was born on 1 June 1907 and died on 9 August 1996.\n- Frank Whittle was an English Royal Air Force engineer air officer and held the rank of Air Commodore.\n- The National Gas Turbine Establishment at Pyestock in Fleet was part of the Royal Aircraft Establishment.\n- The National Gas Turbine Establishment was the prime site in the United Kingdom for the design and development of gas turbine and jet engines.\n- The National Gas Turbine Establishment was created by merging the design teams of Frank Whittle's Power Jets and the Royal Aircraft Establishment turbine development team run by Hayne Constant.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "c0dfe13d-3260-54de-a761-5276a47c1823",
        "text": "Page: National Gas Turbine Establishment. Sentence: The National Gas Turbine Establishment (NGTE Pyestock) in Fleet, part of the Royal Aircraft Establishment (RAE), was the prime site in the UK for design and development of gas turbine and jet engines.\nPage: National Gas Turbine Establishment. Sentence: It was created by merging the design teams of Frank Whittle's Power Jets and the RAE turbine development team run by Hayne Constant.\nPage: Frank Whittle. Sentence: Air Commodore Sir Frank Whittle {'1': \", '2': \", '3': \", '4': \"} (1 June 1907 – 9 August 1996) was an English Royal Air Force (RAF) engineer air officer.",
